meta {
  name: Reconcile payments
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{internal_base}}/internal/reconcile
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{service_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "provider": "TRON_TRC20",
    "sinceMinutes": 60
  }
}

docs {
  Triggers one on-demand reconciliation pass by enqueueing the worker's
  existing sweep — the request itself never talks to a provider API:

    CRYPTOBOT   -> the "payments-poll" queue (re-checks PENDING/CONFIRMING
                   invoices against getInvoices)
    TRON_TRC20  -> the "chain-scan" queue (re-scans deposit addresses on
                   TronGrid)

  Responds 202 with { enqueued, provider, queue, jobId }. Requests within the
  same second collapse into one job (deterministic jobId), so an agent retry
  after a timeout is safe.

  `sinceMinutes` is accepted and carried on the job but ADVISORY today: both
  sweeps re-check every pending row regardless of the window.

  BALANCE and STARS are rejected with 400 — the balance is our own ledger and
  Stars settle synchronously inside Telegram, so neither has an external
  record to disagree with.

  Mismatches the sweep finds are published to the tgshop:events:payments
  stream as `payment.reconcile_mismatch` (see docs/AGENT_PLAN.md capability 3).
}
